"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nConsisting of a total of seven short stories, it goes beyond the simple framework of  and delves into the dark desires of humans hidden in ordinary daily life.  \nAs the title suggests, in a situation where all characters look suspicious, the reader is left questioning what is true and who to trust.  \n\nEvery character has suspicious circumstances and motives. In other words, naturally everyone is a suspect.  \n\nReaders realize how easily they fall into prejudice and make hasty judgments.  \n\nOn what basis do you judge and trust others?"